%% Write path — CSV upload through aggregation
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant APIGW as API Gateway
    participant Upload as Upload Lambda
    participant S3 as S3 (imports bucket)
    participant DDB as DynamoDB (imports table)
    participant EB as EventBridge
    participant Split as Split Lambda
    participant SQS as SQS (processing queue)
    participant Worker as Worker Lambda(s)
    participant Aggregator as Aggregator Lambda

    User->>APIGW: POST /imports (multipart or JSON envelope)
    APIGW->>Upload: invoke (proxy event)
    Upload->>Upload: validateUploadFile (extension, MIME, size)
    Upload->>DDB: saveImport(status=UPLOADED)
    Upload->>S3: putObject incoming/{importId}/{filename}
    Upload-->>APIGW: 201 { importId, status: UPLOADED }
    APIGW-->>User: 201 Created

    S3--)EB: Object Created (key prefix incoming/)
    EB->>Split: async Invoke(event)
    Split->>DDB: getImport(importId)
    Split->>S3: getObject(source CSV)
    Split->>Split: splitCsvIntoChunks(chunkSize)
    Split->>DDB: updateImport(status=SPLITTING, totalChunks, totalRecords)
    loop for each chunk
        Split->>S3: putObject processing/{importId}/chunk-NNNN.csv
        Split->>SQS: SendMessage(ChunkMessage)
    end
    Split->>DDB: updateImport(status=QUEUED, or FAILED if 0 chunks)
    Note right of Split: EventBridge invokes asynchronously, so a Split<br/>failure gets Lambda's built-in async retry, then lands<br/>in the async-failures DLQ if it still doesn't succeed

    par one invocation per SQS batch (up to worker_concurrency)
        SQS->>Worker: batch of ChunkMessage (batchSize 10)
        Worker->>S3: getObject(chunk)
        Worker->>Worker: parseCsvText + validateCustomerRecord (per row)
        Worker->>DDB: saveChunkResult (upsert by chunkNumber, isNewChunk?)
        alt isNewChunk
            Worker->>DDB: incrementProcessedChunks(importId) [atomic ADD]
        else redelivered chunk
            Worker->>DDB: listChunkResults(importId) [use existing count]
        end
        Worker->>DDB: updateImport(status=RUNNING, running totals)
        alt processedChunks == totalChunks
            Worker->>Aggregator: async Invoke({ importId })
            Note right of Worker: only the Worker that observes the atomic<br/>counter reaching totalChunks invokes it —<br/>guards against a double-trigger race
        end
    end

    Aggregator->>DDB: getImport(importId)
    Aggregator->>DDB: listChunkResults(importId)
    alt chunkResults.length < totalChunks
        Note right of Aggregator: aggregation skipped — replay or early<br/>invocation while chunks are still pending
    else all chunks accounted for
        Aggregator->>Aggregator: derive COMPLETED / PARTIAL_SUCCESS / FAILED
        Aggregator->>DDB: updateImport(final status, totals, executionTimeMs)
    end
